On Mon, May 23, 2027 at 9:12 AM Samir Patel <samir@brightleaf.ai> wrote:
> Hi Chloe,
> 
> Thanks for coordinating — excited to get the BrightLeaf chat assistant hooked into Redwood. Lara and I reviewed the onboarding guide and we have two quick asks before the kickoff call: 
> 
> 1) Do you have a lean checklist for SDK install + initial endpoint switch (we'll want to migrate from our current /v1/generate endpoint to the Redwood-hosted endpoint once we're satisfied)?
> 2) We handle patient PII tokens and need recommended default timeouts/retry behavior for 1) short chat-turns (<= 256 tokens) and 2) long context calls (>= 4k tokens) to avoid duplicate messages in our queue.
> 
> Also, we prefer a dry-run cutover where traffic is mirrored for 24 hours. Is that supported?

Hi Samir — great questions. I put together a compact activation checklist and two lean code snippets (Node + Python) that show the recommended SDK initialization and an endpoint switcher pattern for staged migration. See attached: redwood_sdk_samples_v1.zip. I also exported a short mutual action plan PDF for your PM: brightleaf_mutual_action_plan.pdf.

Quick answers up front:
- Dry-run mirror: yes — we support mirrored traffic using our Dedicated sandbox route (we can mirror 10-20% of production traffic for 24 hrs for verification).
- Timeouts & retries (initial defaults):
  • Short turns (<=256 tokens): client timeout = 3s, server RTT buffer = +500ms, retry up to 2x with exponential backoff starting at 250ms.
  • Long calls (>=4k tokens): client timeout = 90s (or 3x typical long-call time), server will return partial results if streaming is used; avoid automatic retries for idempotency concerns — use request dedupe-id and server-side idempotency keys.

I've included a small migration helper that shows how to add a feature-flagged endpoint switch, plus a retry wrapper that supports an idempotency token header. Below is the Node example from the zip (full samples in the attachment).

--- node snippet ---
const Redwood = require('redwood-sdk');
const client = new Redwood.Client({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY, defaultTimeoutMs: 3000 });

async function callGenerate(payload, opts = {}) {
  const idempotencyKey = opts.idempotencyKey || generateId();
  try {
    return await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-mini', input: payload }, { headers: { 'Idempotency-Key': idempotencyKey } });
  } catch (err) {
    // resume-safe retry for short-turns only
    if (shouldRetry(err) && opts.retriesLeft > 0) {
      await sleep(expBackoff(opts.attempt));
      return callGenerate(payload, { ...opts, retriesLeft: opts.retriesLeft - 1 });
    }
    throw err;
  }
}

/* migration switch (pseudocode) */
const USE_REDLWOOD = featureFlag('redwood_switch');
const endpoint = USE_REDLWOOD ? 'https://api.redwood.com/v1/generate' : 'https://internal-old/v1/generate';

--- end snippet ---

